# File descriptions: R CMP optimization

| File or folder | Purpose | Required input | Expected output |
|---|---|---|---|
| `run_CMP_optimization.R` | Main R implementation of the CMP optimization model. It maximizes genetic gain using GCA and SCA while constraining relatedness through target status number `Ns`. | Excel workbook with GCA, SCA, genomic relationship matrix `G`, and optional cross-limit matrix. | Three output sheets are written into the same workbook: `Output_Parents_p`, `Output_Families_Y`, and `Operational_Plan_Simple`. |
| `input_example/input.xlsx` | Example workbook for testing the script. | None; provided as a ready-to-use example. | The same workbook is updated after the script runs. |
| `expected_outputs/` | Output-sheet schemas so users know what to expect before running Gurobi. | Output generated by `run_CMP_optimization.R`. | CSV schema files and README describing each sheet. |

## Input workbook sheet order

| Sheet | Content | Dimension |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | GCA values | `n parents x 1` |
| 2 | SCA matrix | `n parents x n parents` |
| 3 | Genomic relationship matrix `G` | `n parents x n parents` |
| 4 | Optional cross-limit matrix | `n parents x n parents` |

## Example command

```bash
Rscript 01_CMP_optimization/001_R/run_CMP_optimization.R 01_CMP_optimization/001_R/input_example/input.xlsx 5 1000
```

